{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.testing\/documentation\/InnoRouterMacros"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"InnoRouterTesting"},{"type":"text","text":" ships three test stores that mirror the production stores’ public API and transparently subscribe to every public observation callback:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NavigationTestStore"},{"text":" — asserts ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NavigationStore"},{"text":" events (push\/pop\/batch\/transaction\/middleware mutation\/path mismatch).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ModalTestStore"},{"type":"text","text":" — asserts "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ModalStore"},{"type":"text","text":" events (present\/dismiss\/queue\/intercept\/middleware mutation)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FlowTestStore"},{"text":" — asserts ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FlowStore"},{"text":" intents end-to-end, including the inner navigation and modal emissions.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@testable import"},{"type":"text","text":" is required. The harness itself avoids app-side access"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to FlowStore internals; configure inner navigation \/ modal behavior through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FlowStoreConfiguration"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Event queue model","anchor":"Event-queue-model"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each test store owns a FIFO queue. Every time the underlying store emits an observation callback, the corresponding event is appended. Tests consume events in order via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"receive(...)"},{"type":"text","text":" or its typed helpers ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"receiveChange"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"receivePresented"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"receiveIntentRejected"},{"type":"text","text":", and so on). A strict-mode test store fails via Swift Testing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Issue.record"},{"type":"text","text":" if any events are left unasserted at deinit."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift skip doc-fragment","type":"codeListing","code":["import Testing","import InnoRouterTesting","","@Test","@MainActor","func pushHomeLogsChangeEvent() {","    let store = NavigationTestStore<AppRoute>()","    store.send(.push(.home))","    store.receiveChange { old, new in","        old.path.isEmpty && new.path == [.home]","    }","    store.finish()","}"]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Exhaustivity","anchor":"Exhaustivity"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default mode is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TestExhaustivity.strict"},{"type":"text","text":": unasserted events at store deinit (or at an explicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"finish()"},{"type":"text","text":") are reported as test issues. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TestExhaustivity.off"},{"type":"text","text":" preserves the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"receive(...)"},{"type":"text","text":" assertions but silences the final drain check — useful when incrementally migrating large legacy suites."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"User callbacks are preserved","anchor":"User-callbacks-are-preserved"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When you pass a production "},{"code":"NavigationStoreConfiguration","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"ModalStoreConfiguration","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"code":"FlowStoreConfiguration","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" into a test store, every hook (including "},{"code":"onChange","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"onPresented","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"onCommandIntercepted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"onPathMismatch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", etc.) still fires. The test store appends events after the user callback runs, so production middleware and analytics pipelines behave under test exactly as they would in the app."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"End-to-end flow assertions","level":3,"anchor":"End-to-end-flow-assertions","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FlowTestStore"},{"type":"text","text":" subscribes to the inner "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NavigationStore"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ModalStore"},{"type":"text","text":"’s full observation surface and wraps those emissions into "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".navigation(...)"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".modal(...)"},{"type":"text","text":" events on a single queue. This lets a test assert the complete chain triggered by one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FlowIntent"},{"type":"text","text":" — for instance, that a sheet-blocking middleware prevents the inner navigation store from seeing any command:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift skip doc-fragment","code":["let store = FlowTestStore<AppRoute>(","    configuration: FlowStoreConfiguration(","        modal: ModalStoreConfiguration(","            middlewares: [","                ModalMiddlewareRegistration(","                    middleware: BlockSheetMiddleware(),","                    debugName: \"BlockSheet\"","                )","            ]","        )","    )",")","","store.send(.presentSheet(.onboarding))","store.receiveIntentRejected(","    intent: .presentSheet(.onboarding),","    reason: .middlewareRejected(debugName: \"BlockSheet\")",")","store.expectNoMoreEvents()"],"type":"codeListing"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/innoroutertesting\/innoroutertesting"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.testing\/documentation\/InnoRouterTesting\/InnoRouterTesting","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Host-less, Swift-Testing native assertion harness for InnoRouter’s navigation, modal, and flow authorities.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"InnoRouterMacros"}],"role":"collectionGroup","title":"InnoRouterTesting"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Tutorials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.testing\/documentation\/InnoRouterTesting\/Tutorial-TestingFlows"],"anchor":"Tutorials"}],"references":{"doc://com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.testing/documentation/InnoRouterMacros":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/innoroutermacros","role":"collection","title":"InnoRouterMacros","abstract":[],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.testing\/documentation\/InnoRouterMacros"},"doc://com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.testing/documentation/InnoRouterTesting/Tutorial-TestingFlows":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.testing\/documentation\/InnoRouterTesting\/Tutorial-TestingFlows","kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Assert the complete chain triggered by a single "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FlowIntent"},{"type":"text","text":" —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"navigation, modal, middleware cancellation, path reconciliation —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through a single FIFO receive queue, without mounting any SwiftUI"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"host."}],"title":"Testing Flows End-to-End with `FlowTestStore`","url":"\/documentation\/innoroutertesting\/tutorial-testingflows","role":"article"}}}